## Compare before you book
Flights and trains are often cheaper when booked weeks ahead. Compare several sites and the official one.

## Travel off-peak
Midweek and shoulder-season trips usually cost less for transport and stays.

## Choose a place with a kitchen
Cooking some meals saves a lot on longer trips.

## Use local transport
Metros and buses are cheaper than taxis and part of the experience.

## What to watch
Read cancellation rules before paying, so a cheap fare does not become costly if plans change.
